  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math>&nbsp;of gas, the plot of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pV</mi></math> vs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> is shown below. p is the pressure and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is the volume of the gas.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0007_64c46da2d42a.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 281px;\" /></p><p>What is the value of compressibility factor at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>?</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi>RTV</mi></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi>RTV</mi></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to Van der Waals equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>RT</mi></math></p><p>Where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;= molar volume of the gas</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>= Universal gas constant</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>&nbsp;= Temperature</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;= Pressure</p><p>At point A &#39;a&#39; is considerable&nbsp;and &#39;b&#39; is negligible.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>RT</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PV</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>RT</mi></math></p><p>Compressibility factor (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math>) =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mi>RT</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, the correct answer is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi>RTV</mi></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}